; A balance assignment whose target has no commodity posts the single
; amount left: the euros of Netted net out, the other commodity leaves,
; the two lots of Lots are one commodity, and Future's zero is posted
; before its later euros (src/textual_xacts.cc, balance assignment;
; src/balance.h:473-480, balance_t::to_amount).  The semantic
; bisimulation (test/semantic/check_all.py) replays this journal, so an
; oracle that fanned the difference out over the commodities, or that
; rejected it, would fail here.

2024/01/01 Open
    Assets:Netted    $10
    Assets:Netted    20 EUR
    Assets:Future    $10
    Equity:Opening

2024/01/01 Buy one lot
    Assets:Lots    10 FOO @ $1
    Equity:Opening

2024/01/01 Buy another lot
    Assets:Lots    10 FOO @ $2
    Equity:Opening

2024/01/02 Net out the euros
    Assets:Netted    -20 EUR
    Equity:Opening

2024/01/03 Zero an account whose other commodity nets to zero
    Assets:Netted    = 0
    Assets:Cleared

2024/01/03 Zero an account holding two lots of one commodity
    Assets:Lots    = 0
    Assets:Cleared

2024/01/03 Zero an account before a later posting in another commodity
    Assets:Future    = 0
    Assets:Cleared

2024/01/05 Later euros
    Assets:Future    20 EUR
    Equity:Opening

test bal
                 $20
              20 EUR
              20 FOO  Assets
                 $20
              20 FOO    Cleared
              20 EUR    Future
                $-50
             -20 EUR  Equity:Opening
--------------------
                $-30
              20 FOO
end test
